FuncDef:
The reset bgp link-state unicast command resets specified BGP connections.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'all', 'Info': 'Resets all BGP connections.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'as-number', 'Info': 'Resets BGP connections with peers in ASs expressed in dotted notation.\nThe value is in the format of x.y, where x and y are integers that range from 1 to 65535 and from 0 to 65535, respectively.'}
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Resets the BGP connection with a specified peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'ipv6-address', 'Info': 'Resets the BGP connection with a specified IPv6 peer.\nThe value is a 32-digit hexadecimal number, in the format of X:X:X:X:X:X:X:X.'}
{'Parameters': 'external', 'Info': 'Resets all EBGP connections.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'internal', 'Info': 'Resets all IBGP connections.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'group group-name', 'Info': 'Resets the BGP connection with a specified peer group.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
